  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present simple: questions with do/does",
      "title_form": "Preguntas con do/does",
      "title_target": "Questions with Do/Does",
      "description_md_form": "Para hacer **preguntas de sí/no** en presente simple, usamos **do** o **does** al inicio. Usamos **do** con *I, you, we, they* y **does** con *he, she, it*. Después del do/does, el verbo va en su **forma base** (sin -s).\n\n**Estructura:**\n\n- **Do** + sujeto + verbo base?\n- **Does** + sujeto + verbo base?\n\nEjemplos:\n\n- *Do you use bread?* = ¿Usas pan?\n- *Does she have a cat?* = ¿Ella tiene un gato?\n\nPara responder, usamos **yes** o **no** con la forma corta:\n\n- *Yes, I do.* / *No, I don't.*\n- *Yes, she does.* / *No, she doesn't.*",
      "description_md_target": "To make **yes/no questions** in the present simple, we use **do** or **does** at the beginning. We use **do** with *I, you, we, they* and **does** with *he, she, it*. After do/does, the verb goes in its **base form** (without -s).\n\n**Structure:**\n\n- **Do** + subject + base verb?\n- **Does** + subject + base verb?\n\nExamples:\n\n- *Do you use bread?* = Do you use bread?\n- *Does she have a cat?* = Does she have a cat?\n\nTo answer, we use **yes** or **no** with the short form:\n\n- *Yes, I do.* / *No, I don't.*\n- *Yes, she does.* / *No, she doesn't.*",
      "grammar_structure": "Do/Does + subject + base verb + ...?",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "present_simple_questions",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Pregunta",
          "Respuesta corta sí",
          "Respuesta corta no"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "Do I...?",
            "Yes, I do.",
            "No, I don't."
          ],
          [
            "you",
            "Do you...?",
            "Yes, you do.",
            "No, you don't."
          ],
          [
            "he",
            "Does he...?",
            "Yes, he does.",
            "No, he doesn't."
          ],
          [
            "she",
            "Does she...?",
            "Yes, she does.",
            "No, she doesn't."
          ],
          [
            "we",
            "Do we...?",
            "Yes, we do.",
            "No, we don't."
          ],
          [
            "they",
            "Do they...?",
            "Yes, they do.",
            "No, they don't."
          ]
        ]
      },
